NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"2d5cc0862d3ab77d01af18f86be950a8593497f082811494489e0a929e64b456","event_uuid":"cc4da943-f0e3-462d-9b45-3bf3a58d8f2f","position":{"commit_sha":"f1b446ecd0d404ff7bf3a3f6ceac94d9411aab12","position":"1794602463337217057-cc4da943-f0e3-462d-9b45-3bf3a58d8f2f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"af5a6c9b15db5dd99c2a844ad038a5c615a2dbafbdf63a588efd2cd1095b13fb","event_uuid":"aed5ddc6-66e5-41b4-82e3-3886b40dffab","position":{"commit_sha":"c1cb73e5f02746e8a07ffa89e36208428fcb7b3f","position":"1794602599994389048-aed5ddc6-66e5-41b4-82e3-3886b40dffab"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"17a3d3d43ecd90a9023d5da33d1661ff05fbd6644632e4208b57ce3840fb0d42","event_uuid":"0335c05b-4015-4e96-bedb-b9a2461679da","position":{"commit_sha":"7c0eff45cadb34b89e08aca6116b65080c8237fb","position":"1794602754766502804-0335c05b-4015-4e96-bedb-b9a2461679da"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9bf34e221bf22a0db05fef599a19fae5dbddace344cb6d8fd2c13003a459b62c","event_uuid":"22580f9f-d776-450a-a840-2ddd645a88b7","position":{"commit_sha":"4847343be64184ad9c9bce1fedc24211269f07f8","position":"1794602799575943037-22580f9f-d776-450a-a840-2ddd645a88b7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8b6f4c985195166e0d988f713745a25a8aaf7fd3f808a880f5e498833ad1e256","event_uuid":"15895cc1-d873-4768-ab2f-e9e5bffad00d","position":{"commit_sha":"26b41dcbc10cb1ca0f2ef12e5123829f2f09468b","position":"1794602807708330791-15895cc1-d873-4768-ab2f-e9e5bffad00d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"46e074b202cd7fe06d736addd05c1a98ff8241a4a7ccabcab54c81c98982bc82","event_uuid":"9eee719c-fe11-4c05-bd1a-2e9ba4f3510a","position":{"commit_sha":"4165412a8013472777695efbbd595b23310b34bb","position":"1794602810632857510-9eee719c-fe11-4c05-bd1a-2e9ba4f3510a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed as e402300d619 in worktree fix-engine-reuse-docs: ADR 0123 §6 and the 2026-11-13 amendment, docs/plan-review-gate.md §\"Choosing the engine\", and the plan_review_status MCP description (now lists currency_basis and engine) with the tool-surface golden updated. `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check` exits 0, because docs/mcp-reference.md carries only the first sentence. The named test set gave 2613 passed and 1 failed. The failure, test_atomic_completion_close::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle, comes from the agent sandbox denying os.sysconf(\"SC_SEM_NSEMS_MAX\"). It fails the same way on unmodified origin/main inside the sandbox and passes outside it. make verify is running outside the sandbox.","timestamp":1794595873424569606}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794590988900953823,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2b70b75b-3db7-4b95-b44f-5c6a1ac71bf3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561"},{"link_uuid":"8b24f3a2-d0e2-4b17-a1cc-455e70bda4ba","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bd3a-2271-885f-4ffd"},{"link_uuid":"9eee719c-fe11-4c05-bd1a-2e9ba4f3510a","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"5bd7-33ec-8630-440e"}],"description":"## Problem\nADR 0123 §6 (`docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md`, the \"Pipeline-only steps\" bullet) says of the pre-dispatch shortcuts: \"Each reuses or re-signs a pipeline attestation or verdict\", and its \"Why\" list says \"The shortcuts hand back a pipeline attestation or verdict\". That is wrong for 2 of the 3 shortcuts.\n\n`reuse.idempotent_reuse` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py`) is gated by `claim_gate_check` alone, so a pipeline review on a ticket whose current attestation was signed by the **agentic** engine returns the reused PASS (`coverage.idempotent_skip: true`, `runner: \"reused\"`) without running the pipeline. `orchestrator.drift_refresh` likewise re-signs the prior attestation and carries its engine forward (`attest.py`: \"A refresh re-binds the PRIOR verdict, so its engine is still the provenance\"). Only `reuse.verdict_reuse` is engine-matched (it refuses a sidecar whose `coverage.engine` is not `pipeline`).\n\nThat engine-agnostic reuse is the intended design: story `confident-snooty-stinkpot` records it (\"a pipeline run on an agentic-certified ticket reports `idempotent_skip`\"), and `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py::test_an_agentic_pass_certifies_for_a_later_pipeline_review` pins it. The ADR text, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\", which says only that a pipeline run and an agentic run are \"separate jobs\", do not tell a reader that an explicit `engine=pipeline` request can return the agentic result.\n\nObserved on production (aa1681bb531, 2026-11-13 09:19 PST): `review_plan_start` with `engine: \"pipeline\"` on `brocatello-industrial-leafbird`, which held a current agentic attestation, finished with `decided_by_run: false`, the replayed agentic `REVIEW_RESULT`, the unchanged `signed_at`, and `plan_review_status` still reporting `engine: \"agentic\"`. The same reproduces locally with `rebar review-plan <id> --engine pipeline`, which returned `runner: \"reused\"` in 2 s.\n\nA smaller, related gap: the MCP `plan_review_status` tool description (`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`) lists its return as `{ok, verdict, reason, verified_at_sha, signed_at}`, but it also returns `currency_basis` and `engine` (`attest_gate.plan_review_status`), and `engine` is part of ADR 0123 §5's contract.\n\n## Approach\nCorrect the documentation to match the pinned behaviour. Do not change behaviour.\n- ADR 0123 §6: state that `verdict_reuse` replays only a pipeline BLOCK, while `idempotent_reuse` and `drift_refresh` act on the current attestation whichever engine signed it, so a pipeline request on an agentic-certified, unchanged ticket returns the reused agentic PASS, and a drift refresh keeps the attestation's `engine`. Fix the matching \"Why\" bullet. Add a dated line to the 2026-11-13 amendment.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\": add 1 sentence saying the same, and that changing the plan, or `--force`, which only a human operator uses, makes the next review run afresh.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`: list `currency_basis` and `engine` in `plan_review_status`'s documented return, and regenerate `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` with the repo's existing generators if they embed the text.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` (regenerated only)\n\nNo config key, environment variable or flag is added.\n\n## Testing\nThis is a documentation-only fix of pinned behaviour, so no red test is possible: both halves are already pinned by tests that pass on `origin/main`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py::test_an_agentic_pass_certifies_for_a_later_pipeline_review` (cross-engine `idempotent_reuse`) and `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py::test_refresh_carries_the_prior_engine` (drift refresh keeps the prior engine). The corrected text cites them.\n- `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py tests/interfaces -q` exits 0.\n- `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] ADR 0123 §6 no longer says every shortcut reuses only a pipeline attestation. It states that `idempotent_reuse` and `drift_refresh` act on the current attestation under either engine, and that `verdict_reuse` replays only a pipeline BLOCK.\n- [x] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\" states that a pipeline review of an unchanged ticket with a current agentic attestation returns the reused agentic PASS.\n- [x] The `plan_review_status` tool description in `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` lists `currency_basis` and `engine`.\n- [x] `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py tests/interfaces -q` exits 0.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md","reason":"correct §6 shortcut wording"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"state cross-engine attestation reuse in Choosing the engine"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"list currency_basis and engine in plan_review_status description"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json","reason":"regenerated golden for the description change"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","bd3a-2271-885f-4ffd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"22580f9f-d776-450a-a840-2ddd645a88b7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7d68-8e1e-2860-44fc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"ADR 0123 says pipeline shortcuts reuse only pipeline attestations; they reuse agentic ones","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["34bc768b-848b-41d4-91c5-53ca6ec349cf","f5d5268a-51ca-4e51-8a32-951432fad693","ab820c5f-bc50-4662-91ce-c23aebfff1f2","2396b2e2-033b-4d3b-9e4e-37928fdb6367","8b24f3a2-d0e2-4b17-a1cc-455e70bda4ba","cc4da943-f0e3-462d-9b45-3bf3a58d8f2f","aed5ddc6-66e5-41b4-82e3-3886b40dffab","0335c05b-4015-4e96-bedb-b9a2461679da","22580f9f-d776-450a-a840-2ddd645a88b7","15895cc1-d873-4768-ab2f-e9e5bffad00d","9eee719c-fe11-4c05-bd1a-2e9ba4f3510a"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794602810632857511,"uuid":"d2801b5c-1187-4c71-98a7-b6ae8655df4f"}